{"availability":"available","full":"zuemen/carbon-lei","name":"carbon-lei","description":"Checkable carbon-border (CBAM) emissions reports: who signed, were they authorised, and has each verified tonne already been claimed? GLEIF-rooted vLEI credentials plus an Ethereum Sepolia ledger.","category":"Finance","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-09-23T09:49:55Z","updated":"2026-10-11T02:06:30Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://zuemen.github.io/carbon-lei/","topics":["carbon-accounting","cbam","climate","ethereum","keri","sepolia","solidity","supply-chain","verifiable-credentials","vlei"],"demo":"https://zuemen.github.io/carbon-lei/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T02:10:31.001Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T02:10:31.001Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T02:10:31.001Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T02:10:31.001Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A carbon number is only as trustworthy as the person who signed it.","Checkable carbon-border (CBAM) emissions reports: who signed, were they authorised, and has each verified tonne already been claimed? GLEIF-rooted vLEI credentials plus an Ethereum Sepolia ledger.","Judge's 90-second path: open the demo (read-only, no wallet) → press Verify the demo proof on the first screen (it loads the proof on the Buyer tab and runs the eight checks) → Try to break it → card 4: press \"Verify the impostor's proof\"."],"features":["Who signed: the lead auditor's vLEI role credential (a signed statement that this person holds this role at this verification body; vLEIs are specified in ISO 17442-3:2024), is checked against a GLEIF-rooted chain…","Were they authorised: the contract checks, at the block that registers the report, that the body is active and accredited and the auditor is not revoked.","Already claimed? An on-chain ledger deducts each shipment from the report's verified tonnage (500 t in the demo) and rejects a batch claimed twice or a claim beyond what remains.","Without verified actual values, importers fall back on default values with a mark-up. For CN 7318 (screws, bolts, nuts) from Taiwan, the EU's second-largest external source of these goods (20.3% of extra-EU imports by…","Verified values depend on accredited verifiers. In the Commission's state of play of 7 October 2026, 24 EU/EEA national accreditation bodies had agreed to offer CBAM accreditation, 18 were ready to accept applications,…"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/zuemen/carbon-lei/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f3f7a82d777e93b3807d134cf552cad7b3040b0bbcc6666bbc641721c349b95a","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T02:10:31.516Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T02:10:31.516Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"A carbon number is only as trustworthy as the person who signed it.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/zuemen/carbon-lei/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"Inside the CBAM Registry, the verification body issues the report from an EU Login account, and its proof of representation is submitted when that account is requested [17].","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/zuemen/carbon-lei/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"In the official workflow, the verification body issues the report in the Registry from its EU Login account (question 1 above).","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/zuemen/carbon-lei/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"f3f7a82d777e93b3807d134cf552cad7b3040b0bbcc6666bbc641721c349b95a","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/zuemen/carbon-lei/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T02:10:31.517Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-11T02:06:30Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/zuemen/carbon-lei/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T02:10:31.520Z","hash":"f3f7a82d777e93b3807d134cf552cad7b3040b0bbcc6666bbc641721c349b95a","originalBytes":11